    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7977": {
      "title": "Senior Programmer Analyst",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Senior Programmer Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Programmer Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Senior Programmer Analyst FLSA Classification EX Reports to Director, Application Services Salary Range D Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assumes responsibility for Providing high-quality customer technical consultation and support to Ellucian’s Banner products such as Ethos, Banner Extensibility, Ellucian Experience, Banner Self Service, etc. Provides project management, leadership, needs assessment, integration services and the ability to develop a strong working relationship with the University community partners. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range The budgeted starting salary for this position will be $83,409 to $100,000 dependent upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Provides software troubleshooting and break/fix support up to full application development and spans many areas including applications, integrations, and reporting. Provides technical assistance by responding to inquiries regarding errors, problems, or questions with programs; assists users in troubleshooting issues related to Banner modules within the Ellucian Banner product suite. Creates test plans and runs tests to find errors and confirms specifications have been met. Assists with the configuration and maintenance of Banner and related solutions. Preparing and submitting status reports as requested by manager and unit. Supports University users with extensions that satisfy the customer needs that does not come out of the box on Ellucian Products (non-baseline solutions). Interacts with the users and other third-party representatives to translate business requirements into functional specifications for conversions, reporting, interfaces, and customizations. Monitors, tracks, and reports project risks, issues, milestones, and work completed, as well as work that is underway. Provides leadership for the users enabling them to stay on time and on task. Facilitates business process review and application prototyping sessions as well as providing insight into best practice methodologies. Evaluates and modifies systems, where appropriate, relative to the university business practices. Drives university to innovative technology; provides university high-quality business process, change management and other appropriate documentation. Provides direction in developing testing methodology and test scripts for use during upgrades, patch application and customizations. Works with the users to test and confirm modifications and/or updates meet specifications. Provides guidance in the development of user-training strategy, and when appropriate, delivers such training. Mentors and trains less experienced staff and review their work. Designs and writes reports using Argos against an operational data store. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1241P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Requires travel, including overnight stays. Education Associate degree or Two-year University equivalent required . Bachelor’s Degree preferred Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Intermittently sitting, standing, stooping. Light lifting or carrying 25 lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7962 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7989": {
      "title": "Director of Student Onboarding & Success",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Director of Student Onboarding &amp; Success Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of Student Onboarding & Success Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of Student Onboarding & Success FLSA Classification EX Reports to Dean of Students and Associate Vice President for Student Experience Salary Range D Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week Monday - Friday with some nights and weekends Position Summary Provides strategic leadership for the University’s comprehensive new-student experience, guiding students from admission deposit through the completion of their second academic year. Develops, coordinates, and assesses initiatives that support enrollment conversion, successful changeovers, engagement, belonging, and retention. Leads new student orientation, changeover programming, first-year experience initiatives, and second-year success efforts, working closely with the parent and family engagement personnel and academic and student affairs partners to create a seamless student journey. Using institutional data, the identifies students who could benefit from additional support during academic, social, and personal changes, develops targeted interventions, and continuously improves programming to increase orientation participation, yield, student success, and retention. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s goals and mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range Budged starting salary is $66,750 to $77,000, depending upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership Develops and leads the University’s comprehensive onboarding strategy from deposit through the end of the second year. Establishes measurable goals aligned with enrollment, student success, and retention priorities. Leads institutional planning for new-student transitions in partnership with academic and student affairs leadership. Onboarding & Orientation Programs Leads First-Year Orientation, Transfer Orientation, Family Orientation, Opening Weekend, and Winter Orientation. Recruits, trains, and supervises the Orientation Leader program and student staff team. Chairs the Onboarding Committee, coordinating representatives from Admissions, Advising, Registrar, Student Financial Services, Residence Life, Accessibility, Health Services, Public Safety, and Enrollment. Transition & Retention Programming Develops and leads First Six Weeks and Weeks of Welcome programming to sustain engagement after orientation. Designs catch-up pathways for students who miss orientation, mid-year entrants, and transfer students. Develops Sophomore Success initiatives, including a sophomore retreat, involvement and leadership pathways, and re-engagement outreach for at-risk second-year students. Data-Informed Retention Management Monitors orientation registration and attendance in real time; identify no-shows within 24 hours and coordinate immediate outreach. Establishes and tracks attendance as a formal KPI , distinct from registration. Tracks first-year and second-year persistence by orientation participation status and recommend interventions. Produces an annual report on orientation attendance, yield conversion, satisfaction, and retention outcomes. Partnerships Coordinates consistently with Admissions, Academic Advising, Residence Life, Student Engagement, Accessibility, Financial Aid, Health Services, Public Safety, Faculty, Marketing, and Enrollment Management. Supervisory Responsibility Chairs the Onboarding Committee; directly supervises Orientation Leaders, Returning Student Mentors (Red Caps), and a Graduate Assistant (if available). Performs other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1249P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Master’s Degree required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Light lifting or carrying, 25lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7988 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8000": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President For Finance and Controller",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Assistant Vice President For Finance and Controller Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Vice President For Finance and Controller Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Vice President For Finance and Controller FLSA Classification EX Reports to Vice President for Finance and Chief Financial Officer (CFO) Salary Range A Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assumes responsibility for the management of the University of Hartford’s overall financial reporting and internal control structure under the direction of the Vice President for Finance and Chief Financial Officer ( CFO ). Directs and oversees financial reporting in compliance with generally accepted accounting principles as well as regulatory and statutory requirements that support the University’s financial operation and safeguard its assets. Provides management, guidance and direction to Financial Accounting Services, Payroll, and Accounts Receivable Operations. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range Budgeted salary is $160,000 to $175,000, depending upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities This position has frequent visibility to and interaction with the University’s Board or Regents and plays a key role in preparation and reporting during University Sub-Committee meetings. Assumes responsibility for the development, implementation and maintenance of a comprehensive system of internal controls and procedures designed to comply with federal and state requirements, generally accepted accounting principles and institutional policies and procedures. Oversees internal and external audits and preparation of audit reports. Interprets accounting rules and regulatory requirements that pertain to the University, trains staff in the execution of such requirements as well as develops related policies and procedures which are communicated effectively to the University community in a timely manner. Handles highly sensitive information with confidentiality and tact. Provides strong leadership and oversight over the integrated financial accounting system in an effort to ensure the continuous refinement of business processes designed to increase overall efficiencies and effectiveness within processes/systems functions to provide reliable, auditable financial data, that these processes/systems are linked appropriately to other systems throughout the University, and that such processes/systems provide information useful to management for business process re-engineering and for decisions making. Consistently analyzes financial data and presents financial reports in an accurate and timely manner. Clearly communicates monthly, quarterly and annual financial statements and pertinent information to internal constituents as well as external groups. Prepares regulatory and financial reports as well as federal and state tax filings as required to satisfy federal, state and higher education requirements. Prepares, analyzes and/or interprets data for presentations of audit results, financial statements and IRS Form 990 to the appropriate Board Committee(s) throughout the year. Assumes responsibility for the oversight of several institutional business units, including Financial Accounting Services, Payroll and Bursar’s Office. Provides management guidance, direction and evaluation to ensure that the daily operations of these units comply with all regulatory requirements as well as meet the needs of the University community. Develops, implements and maintains the University’s debt policy in an effort to ensure debt compliance with bond covenants. Serves as liaison and/or leads on various University committees as deemed necessary and/or appropriate. Assists the CFO with staffing the Investment, University Resources, and Audit Committees of the Board of Regents and directs the activities associated with the security and investment of the University’s assets and funds. Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with external auditors. Serves as a primary liaison with the University’s independent auditors. Recommends and implements changes with regard to audit findings. Oversees and/or participates in all other external audit activity. Assists the CFO with special ad hoc projects pertaining to highly sensitive issues and performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1251P Working Conditions Normal office situation, requires travel including overnight stays. Education Master’s degree required and/or CPA required Physical Effort Typcially sitting at a desk or table, light lifting or carrying 25 lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. CPA Higher Education experience Knowledge of Banner System Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7999 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
