    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8067": {
      "title": "Clinical/Applied Healthcare Facility Design Assistant Professor (2027 2028)",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Clinical/Applied Healthcare Facility Design Assistant Professor (2027 2028) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Clinical/Applied Healthcare Facility Design Assistant Professor (2027 2028) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. OPTIONAL: USE THIS FOR SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS YOU HAVE FOR APPLICANTS Posting Details Position Information Job Title Clinical/Applied Healthcare Facility Design Assistant Professor (2027 2028) Rank Assistant Professor Salary Range $86,000 - $90,000 Tenure Information Clinical/Applied Job Description SEARCH CHAIR TO POPULATE Directions: The Department of Architecture within the College of Engineering, Technology, and Architecture ( CETA ) at the University of Hartford is seeking to fill a Clinical/Applied Faculty Member position at the rank of Assistant Professor with expertise in healthcare design and architectural design beginning in August 2026. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate architectural design studios/healthcare design studios, electives in healthcare design, Materials and Methods of Construction, and Construction Documents. Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate architectural design studios, electives in healthcare design, Materials and Methods of Construction, and Construction Documents. This faculty member will collaborate with colleagues to coordinate technical course content and learning outcomes with design studios, strengthening the integration of design knowledge, building technology, and professional practice throughout the curriculum. The successful candidate will also lead the development of a healthcare design concentration, including its curricular framework, courses, and learning outcomes. Working with departmental faculty, the department’s Advisory Board, architectural practitioners, and healthcare organizations, this faculty member will develop educational opportunities that prepare students for professional engagement in healthcare design. Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach architectural design studios, healthcare design electives, ADT 232 Materials and Methods of Construction, and ADT 242 Construction Documents, according to departmental needs. Assist with the coordination of technical course content and learning outcomes with design studios to support an integrated curriculum. Lead the development of a healthcare design and associated courses. Build professional partnerships that support guest lectures, design reviews, site visits, internships, and collaborative projects. Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress and professional development. Participate in departmental and college service, curriculum development, program assessment, and student recruitment and retention. Maintain professional engagement, applied scholarship, creative activity, or professional development consistent with the clinical/applied appointment. The initial Clinical/Applied contract is 1-2 years and subsequent longer-term contracts are based on review of performance and the continuing need for the position. With satisfactory reviews, the next appointment is for three years. Following a satisfactory review, a 5-year contract is offered with additional 5-year contracts offered subsequently. Clinical/Applied faculty can submit for promotion to Clinical/Applied Associate Professor and then to Clinical/Applied Professor. The teaching requirement is 24 credits per academic year. Summer teaching opportunities are also available, if desired. The teaching load is reduced by 3 credits for serving as the Graduate Program Director. The specific expectations, assignments, and responsibilities for the position are defined in the final letter of appointment. Required Qualifications Required: Applicants must hold a current, active license to practice architecture at the time they submit their application. Preferred: A professional degree in architecture, preferably a Master of Architecture (M.Arch.). Professional architectural practice experience in North America. Demonstrated professional experience in healthcare facility planning and architectural design, including knowledge of codes, standards, and design guidelines relevant to healthcare facilities. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, and professional partners. Proficiency in building information modeling ( BIM ), particularly Autodesk Revit, and other digital tools used in architectural design and construction documentation. Demonstrated leadership experience in architectural practice, including project or team leadership, mentorship, or management of collaborative initiatives. Teaching experience in architecture or a related field, preferably at the college or university level. Preferred Qualifications Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Teaching Philosophy Statement of Inclusive Excellence As an institution of higher learning, the University of Hartford strives to be more than merely a mirror of the larger society; it should foster learning and encourage the personal growth of students, faculty, and staff in an environment that promotes and celebrates diversity in all of its forms regardless of identifying factors including but not limited to race, sex, age, religion, national origin, socioeconomic status, physical and learning differences, sexual orientation, gender or gender identity. Accordingly, our commitment is to: · Foster an inclusive, equitable, just, and caring community where the unique identities of each person are fully appreciated, respected, and celebrated · Engage in civil discourse, that values diverse intellectual perspectives · Cultivate a campus community reflective of the intersectionality of the larger society while maintaining an environment of safety and respect where all members experience a sense of belonging · Institutionally, stand against acts of hate, intimidation, discrimination, bigotry, violence, and harassment of any kind · Uphold the values of the institution, so that all our members are treated with dignity and respect Our commitment to Inclusive Excellence and Belonging is a strength that results in a vibrant and more engaged campus culture. Teaching Philosophy In the teaching philosophy statement, please share your thoughts and experiences in using active learning strategies, high-impact practices, and evidence-based pedagogical practices, as well as your methods for engaging students and fostering student belonging in the classroom. University Information Students at the University of Hartford find success in a learning environment that both challenges and mentors them. Our academic mission is to engage students in acquiring the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to thrive in, and contribute to, a pluralistic, complex world. At the University of Hartford, we are committed to community. We are an academic community that values integrity, curiosity, creativity, excellence, responsibility, and accomplishment. Enriched by our engagement with, and understanding of, one another, we take pride in our shared traditions and experiences. We are dedicated to building a culture that respects all of its members and celebrates their contributions as we work together to strengthen our community. The full text of our academic mission, vision, and values can be seen at www.hartford.edu. Opportunities for faculty development and support can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/campus-leadership/office-provost/faculty-development/ and a listing of Affinity Networks can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/diversity-inclusion/affinity-groups.aspx College Information The College of Engineering, Technology, and Architecture offers undergraduate Engineering programs in Electrical, Computer, Acoustical and Music, Biomedical, Civil, Mechanical, Aerospace, and Robotics. It also offers undergraduate Engineering Technology programs in Audio, Computer and Electronic, Electromechanical, as well as Architectural Design + Technology. Additionally, the college offers an undergraduate program in Computer Science, Computer Science and Engineering and Construction Management + Technology. The college also offers master’s programs in Computer Science, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, as well as Architecture. The majority of our undergraduate programs are accredited by ABET , including the Architectural Design + Technology program. The Master of Architecture degree is accredited by the National Architectural Accrediting Board ( NAAB ). The University of Hartford is ideally situated in the heart of Connecticut’s “Aerospace Alley,” a registered trademark of the Aerospace Components Manufacturers group, one of the largest and most experienced concentrations of aerospace companies in the world. A sampling of OEM’s near the University include Pratt & Whitney, Collins Aerospace, Kaman Aircraft, and Sikorsky – A Lockheed Martin Company. Many other aerospace manufacturing companies are within a 30-minute drive from campus. The proximity of such a large group of aerospace manufacturing companies to campus provides many opportunities for research and other industry collaborations. A key strength of the architecture programs is its location in the Greater Hartford region, a hub for architecture, engineering, construction, and building technology firms. This unique setting creates valuable opportunities for industry partnerships, experiential learning, internships, and employment pathways for students. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F223P Open Date 08/16/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants OPTIONAL : USE THIS FOR SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS YOU HAVE FOR APPLICANTS Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently or have you ever been a part-time faculty member at the University of Hartford? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Portfolio (includes applicant work & applicant's student work) Optional Documents Unofficial Transcript Teaching Portfolio Samples of Teaching Effectiveness 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8066": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Aerospace Engineering (2027 2028)",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Aerospace Engineering (2027 2028) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Aerospace Engineering (2027 2028) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Aerospace Engineering (2027 2028) Rank Assistant Professor Salary Range $86,000 - $90,000 Tenure Information Tenure Track Job Description The Mechanical, Aerospace, and Acoustical Engineering Department at the University of Hartford invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Aerospace Engineering at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning August 2027. Applicants from all areas of Aerospace Engineering are welcome. The qualified applicants are expected to have a doctoral degree, excellent potential and dedication to teaching, research, service, and professional activities. Applications are sought from candidates who can help the department conduct innovative research and provide world-class engineering education. The Department is especially interested in qualified candidates who can contribute through their research, teaching, and/or service to the diversity and excellence in the academic community. Review of applications will begin by December 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Responsibilities This position supports the development of the ABET accredited undergraduate Aerospace Engineering Program. This is a relatively new program with significant potential for the applicant to help manage and implement changes to the curriculum and continue the growth of the program. Successful candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, as well as related laboratories, collaborate with students on independent research, supervise student projects, and actively participate in service activities. The successful applicant will develop and teach both graduate and undergraduate courses. An active scholarly agenda with peer-reviewed publications, presentations, or other accomplishments is expected for successful tenure and promotion. Service to the department, college, and university will include advising students as a primary academic advisor, overseeing undergraduate research projects, and perhaps serving as the faculty advisor for a student organization. Candidates are encouraged to describe any particular expertise in curriculum development related to diversity, equity, inclusion, justice, and belonging in Aerospace Engineering. Required Qualifications Required: An earned doctorate in Aerospace Engineering or related discipline is required; ABDs will be considered providing they document a degree completion date. Preferred: Strong interest in curriculum development, including both lecture based and laboratory based courses. Strong interest in scholarly activities, pursuing grants, and supervising student research. A bachelor’s degree in aerospace engineering from an ABET -accredited program. Industrial experience in aerospace engineering. Experience or interest in student recruitment, retention, and career preparation. Aerospace engineering teaching experience at an ABET -accredited program with demonstrated ability to provide effective hands-on education. Excellent communication skills Preferred Qualifications Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Teaching Philosophy Statement of Inclusive Excellence As an institution of higher learning, the University of Hartford strives to be more than merely a mirror of the larger society; it should foster learning and encourage the personal growth of students, faculty, and staff in an environment that promotes and celebrates diversity in all of its forms regardless of identifying factors including but not limited to race, sex, age, religion, national origin, socioeconomic status, physical and learning differences, sexual orientation, gender or gender identity. Accordingly, our commitment is to: · Foster an inclusive, equitable, just, and caring community where the unique identities of each person are fully appreciated, respected, and celebrated · Engage in civil discourse, that values diverse intellectual perspectives · Cultivate a campus community reflective of the intersectionality of the larger society while maintaining an environment of safety and respect where all members experience a sense of belonging · Institutionally, stand against acts of hate, intimidation, discrimination, bigotry, violence, and harassment of any kind · Uphold the values of the institution, so that all our members are treated with dignity and respect Our commitment to Inclusive Excellence and Belonging is a strength that results in a vibrant and more engaged campus culture. Teaching Philosophy In the teaching philosophy statement, please share your thoughts and experiences in using active learning strategies, high-impact practices, and evidence-based pedagogical practices, as well as your methods for engaging students and fostering student belonging in the classroom. University Information Students at the University of Hartford find success in a learning environment that both challenges and mentors them. Our academic mission is to engage students in acquiring the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to thrive in, and contribute to, a pluralistic, complex world. At the University of Hartford, we are committed to community. We are an academic community that values integrity, curiosity, creativity, excellence, responsibility, and accomplishment. Enriched by our engagement with, and understanding of, one another, we take pride in our shared traditions and experiences. We are dedicated to building a culture that respects all of its members and celebrates their contributions as we work together to strengthen our community. The full text of our academic mission, vision, and values can be seen at https:// www.hartford.edu . Opportunities for faculty development and support can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/campus-leadership/office-provost/faculty-development/ and a listing of Affinity Networks can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/diversity-inclusion/affinity-groups.aspx College Information Posting Detail Information Posting Number F231P Open Date 08/16/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently or have you ever been a part-time faculty member at the University of Hartford? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Research Philosophy Optional Documents 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8068": {
      "title": "Clinical/Applied Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy (2027-2028)",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Clinical/Applied Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy (2027-2028) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Clinical/Applied Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy (2027-2028) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Clinical/Applied Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy (2027-2028) Rank Assistant Professor Salary Range $76,000 - $86,000 Tenure Information Clinical/Applied Job Description The College of Education, Nursing, and Health Professions at the University of Hartford is seeking to fill a Clinical Applied Track Assistant Professor position ( full-time , 10-month ) in the Doctor of Physical Therapy Program beginning in August 2027 . The successful applicant will teach courses in Pediatric Physical Therapy and other courses within the DPT program curriculum , based on program needs and faculty expertise, as appointed by the Program Director; assignments may change based on departmental needs. There may also be opportunities to teach our innovative general education and interdisciplinary courses within the university. Candidates are expected to pursue an active professional productivity agenda and participate in service activities at the program, department, college and university level. Responsibilities The successful applicant will teach courses in Pediatric Physical Therapy and other courses within the DPT program curriculum , based on program needs and faculty expertise, as appointed by the Program Director; assignments may change based on departmental needs. There may also be opportunities to teach our innovative general education and interdisciplinary courses within the university. The ideal candidate will demonstrate professional productivity as evidenced by sustained excellence and innovation in their clinical/applied practice, contributions to the profession through publications, presentations, or other publicly disseminated work, as well as service to academic, professional, or Hartford area communities. Service to the program, department, college, and university typically includes advising and mentoring students, contributing to student recruitment and retention, partaking in accreditation , serving on program, departmental, and college-level committees, and participation in community and university events. Candidates are expected to demonstrate a commitment to inclusive excellence, which the University defines as an unwavering commitment to fostering a vibrant campus community where every student, staff member, and faculty colleague feels deeply rooted, empowered to flourish, and inspired to achieve their highest potential. Candidates are expected to maintain professional standards, attitude, and performance levels to ensure effective, safe, ethical, and legal performance in all aspects of the position. They are expected to develop and maintain professional relationships with all staff, faculty, and students and to exhibit positive, professional conduct. The initial Clinical/Applied contract is 1-2 years and subsequent longer-term contracts are based on review of performance and the continuing need for the position. Applicants should describe in their letter of intent how their teaching and/or scholarship or their professional practice will advance intercultural competence in all students. Applicants are also expected to describe in their letter of intent how their scholarship and/or professional practice contributes to diverse communities. Required Qualifications Required: An active Physical Therapy license or eligibility for licensure in the State of Connecticut Earned Doctor of Physical Therapy degree (or tDPT) from an accredited university OR a Bachelor’s/Master’s degree in Physical Therapy with an earned academic doctorate. Minimum of 4 years of clinical experience in Pediatric Physical Therapy Preferred: ABPTS Specialist in Pediatrics or in the process of obtaining advanced certifications. An earned academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, etc.) or in the process of obtaining an earned academic degree. Prior experience teaching physical therapy at an accredited college or university. Demonstrate evidence of a commitment to remain active in the related research areas, clinical, or professional practice, including contributing to the profession through presentations, publications or other work; Active participation in local or national physical therapy associations. Preferred Qualifications Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Teaching Philosophy Statement of Inclusive Excellence As an institution of higher learning, the University of Hartford strives to be more than merely a mirror of the larger society; it should foster learning and encourage the personal growth of students, faculty, and staff in an environment that promotes and celebrates diversity in all of its forms regardless of identifying factors including but not limited to race, sex, age, religion, national origin, socioeconomic status, physical and learning differences, sexual orientation, gender or gender identity. Accordingly, our commitment is to: · Foster an inclusive, equitable, just, and caring community where the unique identities of each person are fully appreciated, respected, and celebrated · Engage in civil discourse, that values diverse intellectual perspectives · Cultivate a campus community reflective of the intersectionality of the larger society while maintaining an environment of safety and respect where all members experience a sense of belonging · Institutionally, stand against acts of hate, intimidation, discrimination, bigotry, violence, and harassment of any kind · Uphold the values of the institution, so that all our members are treated with dignity and respect Our commitment to Inclusive Excellence and Belonging is a strength that results in a vibrant and more engaged campus culture. Teaching Philosophy In the teaching philosophy statement, please share your thoughts and experiences in using active learning strategies, high-impact practices, and evidence-based pedagogical practices, as well as your methods for engaging students and fostering student belonging in the classroom. University Information Students at the University of Hartford find success in a learning environment that both challenges and mentors them. Our academic mission is to engage students in acquiring the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to thrive in, and contribute to, a pluralistic, complex world. At the University of Hartford, we are committed to community. We are an academic community that values integrity, curiosity, creativity, excellence, responsibility, and accomplishment. Enriched by our engagement with, and understanding of, one another, we take pride in our shared traditions and experiences. We are dedicated to building a culture that respects all of its members and celebrates their contributions as we work together to strengthen our community. The full text of our academic mission, vision, and values can be seen at https:// www.hartford.edu . Opportunities for faculty development and support can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/campus-leadership/office-provost/faculty-development/ and a listing of Affinity Networks can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/diversity-inclusion/affinity-groups.aspx College Information The College of Education, Nursing and Health Professions ( ENHP ) offers 30 educational offerings, from undergraduate to doctoral programs and certificates, united by a common goal, to provide inclusive, innovative, and engaging scholarly experiences that shape the next generation of leaders in the service professions. Known for partnership work in urban Hartford, as well as internationally in Peru, Brazil, Mexico, and Kenya, the college emphasizes activities that help “promote the well-being of the communities we serve.” Signature annual events bring students, faculty members, and community partners together to network and showcase scholarly works. ENHP embraces diversity, and its role in preparing students and future professionals to address the needs of an increasingly multicultural society including advocating for optimal educational and health outcomes. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F229P Open Date 08/16/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently or have you ever been a part-time faculty member at the University of Hartford? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts of Highest Degree Optional Documents 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
